==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*fleuganą}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|fleogan|flēoġan}} (Modern {{cog|en|fly}}), {{cog|ofs|fliaga|fliāga}} ({{cog|stq|fljooge}}), {{cog|osx|fliogan}} ({{cog|nds|flegen}}), {{cog|odt|fliogan}} ({{cog|nl|vliegen}}), {{cog|goh|fliogan}} ({{cog|de|fliegen}}). Ultimately from {{der|non|ine-pro|*pleuk-}}. Indo-European cognates include {{cog|lt|plaukti|plaũkti}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|flaug|flugu|floginn}}

# to [[fly]]

